{
  "description": "codebase-kg hooks. (1) A PreToolUse search gate, which starts only for Grep, Glob, and shell commands that run a search command (one `if` rule per search word): a Grep/Glob (or shell grep/rg/find) aimed at mapped code is denied with the instruction to query the code graph first. A graph query clears the next gate_credit searches; a search that already names an anchored file, one aimed outside the repo, one that can only match non-source files (plists, images, Xcode project files), and a repeat of a denied search (the same pattern, however reworded) are all free. Inside a subagent the gate adds the instruction as context instead of denying. (2) A PostToolUse nudge on Edit/Write that reminds you to run /codebase-kg:refresh when you edit source no node anchors on, and periodically once enough mapped files have changed. Both honor .claude/codebase-kg.local.md (search_gate, gate_credit, gate_shell_search, post_edit_nudge, nudge_every, root, graph_path), and both no-op when the repo has no graph. The search gate also honors SKIP_KG; the nudge does not. The search-gate credit hook on codebase-kg MCP calls is `async: true` on purpose: it only records that a graph query ran, so the query never waits for it. (3) A PreToolUse push gate on Bash and PowerShell `git *` commands: a `git push` (also `git -C <dir> push`, chained or env-prefixed) is denied while any mapped file is stale against HEAD, with the instruction to run /codebase-kg:refresh, commit the graph and push again; SKIP_KG=1 and a matching KG_STALE_ACK=<n> pass it, --no-verify does not. (4) A SessionStart notice: a repo that committed the vendored checkers but whose clone has no core.hooksPath or diff.codegraph.textconv gets one line naming the install command, and a clone whose graph diff driver names a missing plugin folder gets one line naming /codebase-kg:setup. It never wires a clone — git leaves .git/config out of a clone so that cloning cannot cause code to run, and wiring it automatically would route around that. In a wired clone whose diff driver pins an older codebase-kg release, it moves the pin to the installed release once that tag is published, and prints one line. (5) A SessionStart server start: when nothing answers GET /health on the server_port setting, or an older codebase-kg build does, it starts this build's shared server detached and waits up to 8 s; it prints one line only when the port belongs to another program or the server does not come up. (6) The SessionStart server start also registers the session, and a SessionEnd hook unregisters it: a server that has seen a registered session exits after CODEBASE_KG_SESSION_GRACE seconds (default 300) with none live and no use.",
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Grep|Glob",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(git *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_push_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(grep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(egrep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(fgrep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(rg *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(ripgrep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(ag *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(ack *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(fd *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(find *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "Bash(sudo *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "PowerShell",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(git *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_push_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 20
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(Select-String *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(sls *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(Get-ChildItem *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(gci *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(grep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(egrep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(fgrep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(rg *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(ripgrep *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(ag *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(ack *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(fd *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          },
          {
            "type": "command",
            "if": "PowerShell(find *)",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "mcp__.*codebase[-_]?kg.*",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_search_gate.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10,
            "async": true
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_post_edit_check.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionEnd": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_session_end.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 5
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_server_start.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "statusMessage": "Starting the codebase-kg server",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "startup|resume|clear",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": ". \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/mcp/launch/run/kg_session_start.cmd\"; exit $LASTEXITCODE",
            "timeout": 10
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
